        {
          "text": "By displaying actual damage, he can demonstrate more clearly why defective protective equipment should be discarded.",
          "grammar": "By＋動名詞 / why節 / should be",
          "ja": "実際の損傷を見せることで、欠陥のある保護具をなぜ廃棄すべきなのかをより明確に示すことができます。",
          "type": "inference",
          "points": 40
        },
        {
          "text": "The trainees' focused attention suggests that the damaged helmet serves as an effective and instructive warning.",
          "grammar": "suggest that / serve as",
          "ja": "研修参加者が集中していることから、この損傷したヘルメットが効果的で教訓的な警告例になっていることがうかがえます。",
          "type": "inference",
          "points": 40
        },
        {
          "text": "Protective equipment whose structural integrity has been compromised may fail to provide adequate protection during an accident.",
          "grammar": "関係代名詞whose / 現在完了受動態 / may",
          "ja": "構造的な強度が損なわれた保護具は、事故時に十分な保護機能を果たさない可能性があります。",
          "type": "inference",
          "points": 40
        },
        {
